What:		/sys/module/kshrink_slabd/parameters/enabled
Date:		October 2026
Description:	Runtime boolean switch for CONFIG_KSHRINK_SLABD, when built
		in; defaults to false. Disabling rejects new asynchronous
		requests under the request lock and waits for pending/running
		work and its memcg reference release. Global scan cancels
		pending work and interrupts running iteration at the next
		group boundary; an active shrinker must return first. A successful write of
		false guarantees idle background reclaim on return. The wait
		is freezable and may be interrupted by a signal: on error,
		admission stays disabled but drain is not guaranteed; write
		false again to retry. Invalid input does not change state.
		Freezing can defer completion until thaw; no bounded latency
		is promised. Direct reclaim, drop_caches, severe pressure and
		a busy/unavailable worker remain synchronous. The Kconfig
		option is also off in the default configuration.

What:		/sys/module/kshrink_slabd/parameters/global_scan
Date:		November 2026
Description:	Boolean mode, default false (single-request mode). True
		selects one serial all-memcg scan on an accepted root/global
		kswapd request. Only the accepted call skips synchronous
		reclaim; nonroot, busy, direct and severe-pressure calls do
		not. Change requires admission disabled and pending/running
		work drained; otherwise EBUSY, including repeated writes.
		Invalid input leaves mode unchanged. Shares the existing
		worker and slot. No periodic timer or launch protocol.
